; inquiry-loop-band.fk — the whole chain as one recipe, tracing its own execution.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk observe/inquiry-loop.fk
;
; The input frame is the last witnessed one, 2026-07-23 00:39 (motion 14, tilt out-of-domain,
; light 3), carried as STORED because at 08:38 the phone is off the cable (adb: device not
; found). The framebuffer counts are live regardless — they are the running fkwu's own.
;
; Verdict 255 when, on Go / Rust / TypeScript / fkwu:
;     1  the stored frame reads as held
;     2  a moving frame reads as moving — the loop tracks state change
;     4  held grounds to the world-frame bearing question
;     8  and the grounded inquiry is stamped stored, not live
;    16  a live frame is stamped live — freshness is carried, not assumed
;    32  the traced run returns a grounded inquiry
;    64  and a framebuffer report from the same window
;   128  whose outcome inherits the frame's freshness — the observation is as honest as the
;        thing observed
;
; The teaching: the diagnostic is not beside the computation, it is the computation, counted
; by the kernel that ran it. And bit 128 is the discipline that makes self-tracing worth
; anything — a recipe that observes itself must carry the freshness of its input all the way
; into its own trace, or it produces a confident record of a stale truth.

(do
    (inquiry-loop-check))
